1. DEFINITIONS

1.1. "Licensor"

"Licensor" means PHMZ, the copyright holder, or any person or
entity expressly authorized by PHMZ to grant rights under this
License.

1.2. "Software"

"Software" means the software, source code, object code, binaries,
documentation, configuration files, build scripts, assets, and
other materials distributed by the Licensor under this License.

1.3. "Source Code"

"Source Code" means the preferred form of the Software for making
modifications, including all source files, interface definitions,
build scripts, configuration files, dependency declarations,
generation scripts, and other materials reasonably necessary to
study, modify, build, test, and reproduce the Software.

Source Code must not be intentionally withheld, obfuscated, or
provided only in a form that materially prevents modification.

1.4. "Modified Work"

"Modified Work" means any work based on, derived from, or
containing the Software or any substantial portion of the Software,
where one or more files, functions, modules, components, interfaces,
behaviors, or other substantial elements have been modified,
translated, extended, adapted, or otherwise changed.

1.5. "Combined Product"

"Combined Product" means any product, application, service,
distribution, system, appliance, package, platform, or other
work that:

(a) incorporates the Software or a substantial portion of it;

(b) links to, embeds, bundles, integrates, or combines the Software
    with other software;

(c) modifies or extends the Software;

(d) uses the Software as a substantial functional component;

(e) is designed, marketed, distributed, or supplied as a unified
    product together with the Software; or

(f) would reasonably be understood by a recipient as a product
    incorporating or based upon the Software.

A Combined Product does not automatically include an independent
and separate work that is merely distributed alongside the Software
without being combined with it, provided that the separate work does
not incorporate, depend upon, extend, or form an integrated part of
the Software.

1.6. "Distribute"

"Distribute" means to make the Software, a Modified Work, or a
Combined Product available to another person or entity, including
by sale, transfer, download, hosting, delivery, publication,
deployment, installation, provision of access, or any other method.

1.7. "Commercial Use"

"Commercial Use" means any use, activity, transaction, arrangement,
or deployment involving the Software, a Modified Work, or a
Combined Product that directly or indirectly provides, enables,
supports, promotes, or contributes to a monetary or non-monetary
benefit to the user or any third party.

Commercial Use includes, without limitation:

(a) selling or reselling;

(b) licensing, sublicensing, leasing, renting, or transferring
    rights for consideration;

(c) providing paid or revenue-generating services;

(d) maintenance, repair, troubleshooting, or technical support
    provided for compensation or commercial advantage;

(e) upgrades, updates, patches, customization, integration,
    migration, or implementation provided for compensation or
    commercial advantage;

(f) reproduction, packaging, bundling, or distribution as part of
    a commercial product or service;

(g) advertising, marketing, promotion, sponsorship, or monetized
    content involving the Software;

(h) installation, deployment, configuration, or operation provided
    for compensation or commercial advantage;

(i) hosting, Software-as-a-Service, Platform-as-a-Service,
    Infrastructure-as-a-Service, managed services, or remote access;

(j) using the Software within an organization, company, business,
    institution, or other entity where the use directly or
    indirectly contributes to revenue, cost reduction, operational
    advantage, customer acquisition, competitive advantage,
    business continuity, or any other economic benefit;

(k) using the Software to create, operate, support, or improve a
    commercial product, commercial service, or commercial activity;

(l) receiving money, goods, services, credits, benefits, discounts,
    consideration, or any other thing of economic value; or

(m) enabling, assisting, facilitating, or causing a third party to
    obtain any of the benefits described above.

Commercial Use may exist even if:

(a) the Software itself is provided without charge;

(b) no payment is made directly to the user;

(c) the benefit is received indirectly;

(d) the Software is only one component of a larger product or
    service; or

(e) the activity is described as free, open, educational, charitable,
    experimental, or internal.

1.8. "Non-Commercial Use"

"Non-Commercial Use" means use that does not constitute Commercial
Use under Section 1.7.

Examples may include personal use, private study, independent
research, experimentation, hobby projects, and non-commercial
educational activities, provided that the activity does not
otherwise generate or facilitate a direct or indirect commercial
benefit.

1.9. "Educational Activity"

"Educational Activity" means teaching, learning, classroom
instruction, academic demonstration, tutorial creation, technical
documentation, or educational presentation.

An Educational Activity does not constitute Commercial Use solely
because the educational institution, instructor, platform, or
course provider charges tuition, admission, subscription, or other
fees.

This exception does not apply where the Software is used to provide
paid installation, consulting, maintenance, customization, hosting,
support, or another commercial service disguised as education.

1.10. "Corresponding Source"

"Corresponding Source" means the complete Source Code of the
Software, Modified Work, or Combined Product that is necessary for
a recipient to study, modify, build, test, and reproduce the
distributed work.

