6. COPyleft AND SAME-LICENSE REQUIREMENT

6.1. General Rule

Any Modified Work, Derivative Work, or Combined Product that is
based on, incorporates, contains, links to, embeds, extends, adapts,
or otherwise materially uses the Software must be licensed as a
whole under this License when Distributed.

6.2. Same License

Every recipient of a Modified Work, Derivative Work, or Combined
Product must receive the same rights and obligations under this
License.

You must not relicense, dual-license, sublicense, or distribute any
such work under terms that are inconsistent with, weaker than, or
different from this License, unless expressly authorized in a
separate written agreement by the Licensor.

6.3. Entire Combined Product

The entire Combined Product, including all components that form part
of the integrated product, must be made available under this License.

This requirement applies to, without limitation:

(a) original components created for the Combined Product;

(b) modified components;

(c) extensions and plugins;

(d) linked and embedded components;

(e) application code;

(f) libraries and modules;

(g) scripts and configuration files;

(h) build and deployment materials;

(i) user-interface components;

(j) service-side and client-side components; and

(k) any other component that forms an integrated or functional part
    of the Combined Product.

6.4. No Proprietary Parts

You must not distribute a Combined Product in which any component
covered by Section 6 is:

(a) closed source;

(b) distributed under proprietary terms;

(c) distributed under a license that prohibits source-code access,
    modification, or redistribution;

(d) subject to technical restrictions that prevent lawful study,
    modification, rebuilding, or redistribution; or

(e) intentionally separated or isolated for the purpose of avoiding
    the obligations of this License.

6.5. Corresponding Source

For every Modified Work, Derivative Work, and Combined Product that
is Distributed, you must provide the complete Corresponding Source
for the entire covered work.

The Corresponding Source must be sufficient for recipients to study,
modify, build, test, and reproduce the complete covered work.

6.6. License Notice

Every Distributed Modified Work, Derivative Work, and Combined
Product must:

(a) include a complete copy of this License;

(b) retain all copyright and license notices;

(c) clearly state that the work is based on Software licensed by PHMZ;

(d) identify significant modifications; and

(e) state that the complete work is distributed under this License.

6.7. No Circumvention

You must not avoid the requirements of this Section by:

(a) placing covered components in separate packages;

(b) distributing components through separate repositories;

(c) using proprietary wrappers or loaders;

(d) replacing direct integration with an equivalent technical
    mechanism intended to evade this License;

(e) claiming that a unified product consists of unrelated works; or

(f) using any other arrangement whose primary purpose is to avoid
    the same-license and source-disclosure requirements.

6.8. Independent and Merely Accompanying Works

A work is not subject to the obligations of this Section merely
because it is:

(a) distributed in the same archive, installer, repository,
    download, storage medium, or distribution channel;

(b) listed in the same project, organization, package index,
    marketplace, or documentation;

(c) distributed alongside the Software;

(d) installed on the same device or system; or

(e) used by the same person or organization.

A work is subject to the obligations of this Section if it is
materially based on, derived from, incorporates, embeds, links to,
extends, adapts, depends upon, or forms an integrated or functional
part of the Software or a Combined Product.

The separation of a component into a different file, module,
package, repository, process, service, container, executable,
repository, or distribution channel does not by itself establish
that the component is independent.

A genuinely independent work that does not incorporate, depend upon,
extend, or form an integrated or functional part of the Software is
not automatically subject to this Section solely because it is
distributed alongside the Software.

6.9. Written Exceptions

The Licensor may grant a written exception to any requirement in
this Section.

No exception is valid unless expressly granted in writing by the
Licensor.

